# Waterfront quay, stone-repair staging; evening return to the lower quarter.
# A harbor-side laborer: flat, unhurried refusal; the discipline of not looking.
NPC: harbor_observer
LOCATION: waterfront
SCHEDULE: morning=quay_repair, midday=quay_repair, evening=lower_house_3, night=lower_house_3

TOPIC: default
  GATE: NOT topic_done(harbor_observer, default) AND coat = plain
  TAG: observer_default_plain
  [The laborer chips mortar from a sea-wall block with a cold chisel, his ring flashing dull umber in the salt air.]
  [He does not look up when Walter stops beside the staging.]
  VOICE: trombone_neutral_medium_v1
  MANUEL SILVA: "High water comes at quarter past five.\nIf you're going to stand on that timber in wool, mind the moss."

TOPIC: default
  GATE: NOT topic_done(harbor_observer, default)
  TAG: observer_default_badge
  [The laborer chips mortar from a sea-wall block with a cold chisel, his ring flashing dull umber in the salt air.]
  VOICE: trombone_neutral_medium_v1
  MANUEL SILVA: "High water comes at quarter past five, Officer.\nIf you're going to stand on that timber, watch your step."

TOPIC: default
  GATE: visit_count(harbor_observer) >= 2 AND NOT (topic_done(harbor_observer, estate_grounds_crew) AND topic_done(harbor_observer, drowned_island) AND topic_done(harbor_observer, the_ring)) AND coat = plain
  TAG: observer_repeat_plain_chisel
  WEIGHT: 3
  [The chisel strikes the granite seam with a flat, dull ring.]
  VOICE: trombone_neutral_short_v1
  MANUEL SILVA: "High water comes at quarter past five. Watch your step on the timber."

TOPIC: default
  GATE: visit_count(harbor_observer) >= 2 AND NOT (topic_done(harbor_observer, estate_grounds_crew) AND topic_done(harbor_observer, drowned_island) AND topic_done(harbor_observer, the_ring)) AND coat = plain
  TAG: observer_repeat_plain_stone
  WEIGHT: 2
  VOICE: trombone_neutral_medium_v2
  MANUEL SILVA: "A sensible man doesn't ask twice about stone he doesn't own."

TOPIC: default
  GATE: visit_count(harbor_observer) >= 2 AND NOT (topic_done(harbor_observer, estate_grounds_crew) AND topic_done(harbor_observer, drowned_island) AND topic_done(harbor_observer, the_ring)) AND coat != plain
  TAG: observer_repeat_badge_timber
  WEIGHT: 3
  VOICE: trombone_bureaucratic_short_v2
  MANUEL SILVA: "A brass badge won't stop the surge from taking the staging out from under you, Officer."

TOPIC: default
  GATE: visit_count(harbor_observer) >= 2 AND NOT (topic_done(harbor_observer, estate_grounds_crew) AND topic_done(harbor_observer, drowned_island) AND topic_done(harbor_observer, the_ring)) AND coat != plain
  TAG: observer_repeat_badge_chisel
  WEIGHT: 2
  [He chips mortar with deliberate force, sending gray dust across Walter's boots.]
  VOICE: trombone_dismissive_short_v2
  MANUEL SILVA: "The precinct doesn't pay wharf repair. Stand back."

TOPIC: default
  GATE: topic_done(harbor_observer, estate_grounds_crew) AND topic_done(harbor_observer, drowned_island) AND topic_done(harbor_observer, the_ring) AND coat = plain
  TAG: observer_exhausted_plain_mud
  WEIGHT: 3
  [He chips mortar with steady, measured strokes, his anchor ring gleaming dull umber.]
  VOICE: trombone_haunting_medium_v1
  MANUEL SILVA: "We leave the mud where it settled, Walter. You should do the same."

TOPIC: default
  GATE: topic_done(harbor_observer, estate_grounds_crew) AND topic_done(harbor_observer, drowned_island) AND topic_done(harbor_observer, the_ring) AND coat = plain
  TAG: observer_exhausted_plain_tide
  WEIGHT: 2
  VOICE: trombone_neutral_short_v2
  MANUEL SILVA: "The tide is making. Go home."

TOPIC: default
  GATE: topic_done(harbor_observer, estate_grounds_crew) AND topic_done(harbor_observer, drowned_island) AND topic_done(harbor_observer, the_ring) AND coat != plain
  TAG: observer_exhausted_badge_quarry
  WEIGHT: 3
  VOICE: trombone_dismissive_short_v1
  MANUEL SILVA: "The town has no business with drowned granite, Officer. Take the uniform up the hill."

TOPIC: default
  GATE: topic_done(harbor_observer, estate_grounds_crew) AND topic_done(harbor_observer, drowned_island) AND topic_done(harbor_observer, the_ring) AND coat != plain
  TAG: observer_exhausted_badge_surge
  WEIGHT: 2
  VOICE: trombone_cautious_short_v1
  MANUEL SILVA: "The surge is in the slipway. Move along, Corwin."

TOPIC: estate_grounds_crew
  GATE: always
  TAG: observer_estate_crew
  LABEL: "Ask about the laborers who work the Ophion grounds"
  TIME: 7
  WALTER CORWIN: "The men who tend the hedges near the kitchen wing at the estate.\nThey come from down here."
  VOICE: trombone_neutral_short_v2
  MANUEL SILVA: "Harbor people work where there's coin."
  WALTER CORWIN: "None of them would go within thirty feet of the pantry door."
  [The chisel pauses on a granite edge, perfectly balanced.]
  VOICE: trombone_neutral_medium_v1
  MANUEL SILVA: "A sensible man doesn't put his hand where the stone is soft."
  WALTER CORWIN: "The stone wasn't soft. It was dry granite."
  VOICE: trombone_haunting_medium_v1
  MANUEL SILVA: "Granite rots too, if you give it reasons.\nWe mend what holds boats. What sits beneath cellars isn't our trade."
  NOTEBOOK: observer_pantry_refusal | "Manuel Silva, asked about the harbor men on the estate crew who won't go near the pantry door: 'A sensible man doesn't put his hand where the stone is soft.'"
  EVIDENCE: observer_stone_discipline

TOPIC: drowned_island
  GATE: evidence(observer_stone_discipline)
  TAG: observer_island
  LABEL: "Ask about the drowned island off the point"
  TIME: 7
  WALTER CORWIN: "Nobody takes dories out to the old whaling ruins anymore."
  VOICE: trombone_dismissive_short_v1
  MANUEL SILVA: "Nothing out there to catch."
  WALTER CORWIN: "There's a chimney standing up out of the mud. Somebody built a station out there once."
  VOICE: trombone_neutral_short_v2
  MANUEL SILVA: "Somebody did."
  [He resumes chipping, steady, flat strikes without anger or haste.]
  VOICE: trombone_haunting_long_v2
  MANUEL SILVA: "My grandfather never went out past the point. Neither did his.\nWe leave the mud where it settled."
  NOTEBOOK: observer_island_1 | "Manuel Silva on the drowned island: three generations of his family have not gone out past the point. 'We leave the mud where it settled.' He offered nothing further."
  EVIDENCE: island_memory

TOPIC: the_ring
  GATE: coat = plain
  TAG: observer_ring
  LABEL: "Ask about the ring on his hand"
  [The mason turns his hand slightly: a flattened copper ring, worn smooth by decades of granite work.]
  WALTER CORWIN: "That ring. I've seen the same on others down here."
  VOICE: trombone_neutral_medium_v1
  MANUEL SILVA: "An anchor link, beaten flat. My father wore it. His father before him."
  WALTER CORWIN: "What's it for?"
  [He looks at the ring, then at Walter, and goes back to the stone.]
  VOICE: trombone_bureaucratic_long_v2
  MANUEL SILVA: "It's for wearing, Officer.\n\nYou ask a great many questions.\nYou should ask yourself sometime whether you're trying to solve this town or just trying to become the next thing it forgets."
  NOTEBOOK: observer_ring_1 | "Manuel Silva wears a flattened copper anchor link as a ring, passed father to son for three generations. He would not say what it was for, and warned Walter against asking too far."
  EVIDENCE: observer_color_tell

